00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:44.757
And hopefully we did wash.
We did wash,

00:19:44.757 --> 00:19:46.563
and we just started, you know,

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:49.590
start over with a clean
slate, in the morning.

00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:51.823
We woke up, both feeling better.

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:55.763
Her issues were behind her.

00:19:59.049 --> 00:19:59.882
Now you're trying.

00:20:03.724 --> 00:20:04.890
And it started raining

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:05.723
Ey.

00:20:05.723 --> 00:20:07.003
A lot.
Ooh.

00:20:07.983 --> 00:20:11.790
It wasn't, it wasn't like
a hurricane or anything-

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:13.320
But there was like,

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:14.153
But it was a lot rain.

00:20:14.153 --> 00:20:16.120
The most rain, in a
shortest period of time,

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:17.960
that Northern California has ever seen.

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:21.233
Well, yeah, in the Central coast, it was,

00:20:21.233 --> 00:20:23.740
they called it like a bomb storm.

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:26.110
Like the word bomb was part of it.

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:27.645
Yeah. I can't remember what it was,

00:20:27.645 --> 00:20:28.478
but yeah, it was nuts.

00:20:28.478 --> 00:20:30.780
And so we got out,

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:33.240
we got some coffee, across the
street, with our umbrellas,

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:35.020
we come back to the room,

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:38.533
and it's, I mean, we got this nice cabin.

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:41.600
We got nothing to do, but each other.

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:42.550
Hm.

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:45.703
And so it was actually,
it was actually perfect.

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:50.180
We were, I mean, that's what we did,

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:51.360
each other.

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:53.000
And with nowhere else to go,

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.720
with nowhere else to be.

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:57.333
I mean, a lot of times
when you go on a vacation,

00:20:58.460 --> 00:20:59.800
you know, there's things you want to do,

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:02.570
there's things you want
to tick off the checklist.

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:04.063
There's people that you're
going to hang out with,

00:21:04.063 --> 00:21:05.730
that maybe you're traveling with,

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:08.620
like your brother and sister-in-law.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:09.453
Yeah.

00:21:09.453 --> 00:21:12.210
Like without any of that
and with no kids around,

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:17.210
it was like a glorious
focus on just the two of us.

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.333
And it was-

00:21:18.333 --> 00:21:19.320
Better than a puzzle, for sure.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:20.443
And let me tell you,

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:24.353
the rain made it an amazing experience.

00:21:24.353 --> 00:21:25.690
Did you go outside?

00:21:25.690 --> 00:21:27.117
The Judds have a song,

00:21:27.117 --> 00:21:29.000
"Rockin' to the rhythm of the rain",

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:30.330
Oh yeah. The Judds.

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:31.220
That's a good song.

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:33.322
The Judds will get me going anytime.

00:21:33.322 --> 00:21:34.710
We didn't play The Judds,

00:21:34.710 --> 00:21:35.770
but I did think about it,

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:38.250
as we were rocking to
the rhythm of the rain.

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:41.380
We didn't go outside, to-

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:44.410
Make love in the rain?
To make love in the rain.

00:21:44.410 --> 00:21:46.520
We stayed in this amazing cabin.

00:21:46.520 --> 00:21:49.053
And then we were like, you know what?

00:21:50.110 --> 00:21:53.280
Let's just lay here
and listen to the rain.

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:55.670
I was playing some music
at a certain point,

00:21:55.670 --> 00:22:00.670
that was like, ambient sounds,
that complimented the rain,

00:22:01.010 --> 00:22:02.813
but I just killed that noise.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:05.700
Yeah. I mean, you know, if you,

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:08.173
if you tell your smart speaker,

00:22:08.173 --> 00:22:11.550
or your sleep device or
whatever, to play rain sounds-

00:22:11.550 --> 00:22:12.606
Yep.

00:22:12.606 --> 00:22:15.050
This is a legitimate, top tier way,

00:22:15.050 --> 00:22:16.910
to relax and go to sleep.

00:22:16.910 --> 00:22:18.450
Oh yeah.
It's manufactured,

00:22:18.450 --> 00:22:21.240
and it comes out of your smart speakers.

00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:22.073
Right.

00:22:22.073 --> 00:22:23.470
I think for the first time in my life,

00:22:23.470 --> 00:22:28.470
I experienced it in
its most pristine form.

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:29.480
The night before-

00:22:29.480 --> 00:22:30.750
You've never heard the rain on the roof?

00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:32.830
Well, the night before we noticed,

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:36.150
that we weren't in a Redwood
grove, where we were,

00:22:36.150 --> 00:22:38.713
we were in an actually an Oak Grove,

00:22:39.898 --> 00:22:42.950
and acorns would fall and
hit the roof of our cabin,

00:22:42.950 --> 00:22:45.030
and scare the shit out of us,

00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:49.490
because of the problems we
were having, that first night.

00:22:49.490 --> 00:22:51.874
Because it was just so loud.

00:22:51.874 --> 00:22:52.707
Mm.

00:22:52.707 --> 00:22:53.540
And it was,

00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:55.320
I thought someone was knocking on the,

00:22:55.320 --> 00:22:57.270
well, somebody was walking on the roof.

00:22:58.400 --> 00:23:00.240
One foot at a time.

00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:01.690
But then when you add,

00:23:01.690 --> 00:23:03.670
when you replace that with rain,

00:23:03.670 --> 00:23:06.670
it was a literal sound bath.

00:23:06.670 --> 00:23:10.430
And it was an amazing
experience, just to lay there,

00:23:10.430 --> 00:23:12.870
and it was so meditative.

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:13.703
I mean,

00:23:13.703 --> 00:23:15.720
to have that thing that you can pull up,

00:23:15.720 --> 00:23:16.800
on a YouTube video,

00:23:16.800 --> 00:23:18.900
so that you can study or fall asleep,

00:23:18.900 --> 00:23:21.973
to experience that in
its most natural form.

00:23:22.940 --> 00:23:23.773
I, yeah,

00:23:23.773 --> 00:23:28.020
I had never experienced a legitimate rain-

00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:29.273
On a hot tin roof?
serenade.

00:23:30.525 --> 00:23:33.187
It was, I mean, it was a, it
was a highlight of my life.

00:23:34.690 --> 00:23:37.710
Especially sexing, in the rain, man.

00:23:37.710 --> 00:23:39.710
That was amazing.

00:23:39.710 --> 00:23:42.350
I know how you tend to get enthusiastic,

00:23:42.350 --> 00:23:43.863
about things like this.

00:23:44.740 --> 00:23:47.070
'Cause I make a decision,

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:49.577
to drink in life, in
those moments and say,

00:23:49.577 --> 00:23:50.560
"You know what?

00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:52.540
It doesn't get any better than this,

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:53.407
other things are going to be",

00:23:53.407 --> 00:23:55.374
And this is me talking,

00:23:55.374 --> 00:23:56.951
Wait no, that's what I'm
saying, that's what I'm saying.

00:23:56.951 --> 00:23:57.876
I'm trying to figure out-

00:23:57.876 --> 00:23:58.790
"It doesn't get any better than this.

00:23:58.790 --> 00:23:59.850
Things have gotten this good,

00:23:59.850 --> 00:24:02.237
but nothing is going to
get better than this."

00:24:03.110 --> 00:24:04.930
You make a decision to do it,

00:24:04.930 --> 00:24:07.147
but you also make a decision
to say that you're doing it,

00:24:07.147 --> 00:24:08.940
and to try to get everybody
else to do it too.

00:24:08.940 --> 00:24:11.560
So I'm just saying, was
Christy, like, "Yeah, I'm"-

00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:13.340
Oh, she was, she was with-

00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:14.660
Or was she shaking her head at you.

00:24:14.660 --> 00:24:16.060
She was with me.

00:24:16.060 --> 00:24:18.200
I mean, it was really magical.

00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:22.060
I think she, you know, she's
taken up the reins too.

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:23.197
I mean, no one wants to be like,

00:24:23.197 --> 00:24:27.300
"Hey, listen, you need to just, I get it.

00:24:27.300 --> 00:24:28.790
This is awesome,

00:24:28.790 --> 00:24:31.680
but I don't need you to
tell me that it's awesome."

00:24:31.680 --> 00:24:33.080
I do understand that.

00:24:33.080 --> 00:24:34.570
And I wasn't doing it forever.

00:24:34.570 --> 00:24:37.602
I mean, we literally just laid there.

00:24:37.602 --> 00:24:41.353
And listened to the rain.

00:24:47.852 --> 00:24:48.952
For how long.

00:24:48.952 --> 00:24:50.477
I don't want to ever forget it.

00:24:50.477 --> 00:24:53.150
Definitely over an hour.

00:24:53.150 --> 00:24:57.840
And this is after many hours
of intense love making.

00:24:57.840 --> 00:25:00.120
Oh man, give me a break.

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:01.930
No, it wasn't many hours, but it,

00:25:01.930 --> 00:25:05.390
when you don't have anything
else to do, besides each other,

00:25:05.390 --> 00:25:06.840
you can stretch everything out.

00:25:06.840 --> 00:25:09.370
And it's nice to get
reacquainted with that,

00:25:09.370 --> 00:25:11.690
and say, "Hey, Remember on our honeymoon,

00:25:11.690 --> 00:25:13.941
when we did it so much that we could,

00:25:13.941 --> 00:25:15.229
we were walking like Cowboys?"

00:25:16.303 --> 00:25:17.136
"Let's see if we can match that."

00:25:17.136 --> 00:25:18.536
Yeah.

00:25:18.536 --> 00:25:23.100
Let's see if we can
have multiple check-ins.

00:25:23.100 --> 00:25:23.933
Yeah.

00:25:23.933 --> 00:25:25.217
But you find yourself saying,

00:25:25.217 --> 00:25:26.310
"Hey, let's actually,

00:25:26.310 --> 00:25:28.640
you know what? Let's just
listen to the rain for an hour."

00:25:28.640 --> 00:25:32.100
It might take me that long to, to re up.

00:25:32.100 --> 00:25:34.780
Well, after that first
session, perspective changes.

00:25:34.780 --> 00:25:37.610
The rain cleared up by mid afternoon,

00:25:37.610 --> 00:25:40.060
and we went back to the place,

00:25:40.060 --> 00:25:41.620
that you guys had recommended,

00:25:41.620 --> 00:25:44.690
that we had been before,
called Nepenthe, or,

00:25:44.690 --> 00:25:46.180
it's right on the coast.
Yeah.

00:25:46.180 --> 00:25:48.250
It's like, there's a
bookstore and a restaurant.

00:25:48.250 --> 00:25:49.850
And you sit on the back of the restaurant,

00:25:49.850 --> 00:25:51.199
and you over,

00:25:51.199 --> 00:25:53.210
Beautiful view.
You just look at the view,

00:25:53.210 --> 00:25:54.043
Look at the ocean.

00:25:54.043 --> 00:25:55.310
It's absolutely amazing.

00:25:55.310 --> 00:25:57.440
We saw an amazing sunset.

00:25:57.440 --> 00:26:00.290
And we were like talking to the waiter,

00:26:00.290 --> 00:26:01.820
like making friends,

00:26:01.820 --> 00:26:04.123
laughing louder than anybody else there.

00:26:04.960 --> 00:26:05.793
You know?

00:26:05.793 --> 00:26:09.760
Again, like I said, last
episode, it's just like,

00:26:09.760 --> 00:26:12.527
just feeling in the zone, feeling like,

00:26:12.527 --> 00:26:16.220
"Oh, look, we're having the
most fun. We're connecting."

00:26:16.220 --> 00:26:19.680
We're like, "It feels like
we're on our honeymoon again."

00:26:19.680 --> 00:26:22.450
And we're watching this beautiful sunset,

00:26:22.450 --> 00:26:25.590
and I look over at Christy's purse,

00:26:25.590 --> 00:26:28.650
and it had been up on the,

00:26:28.650 --> 00:26:29.750
we were sitting at a bar,

00:26:29.750 --> 00:26:31.580
so we could both sit shoulder to shoulder,

00:26:31.580 --> 00:26:33.140
and watch the sunset,

00:26:33.140 --> 00:26:35.220
like that was the best seat in the house.

00:26:35.220 --> 00:26:37.173
And up on that bar,

00:26:38.464 --> 00:26:40.260
her bag was open,

00:26:40.260 --> 00:26:43.973
and it turns out something
was spilling out of it.

00:26:43.973 --> 00:26:45.810
And every time that anyone walked by,

00:26:45.810 --> 00:26:47.980
or the person sitting
right beside Christy,

00:26:47.980 --> 00:26:48.813
on the other side,

00:26:48.813 --> 00:26:50.750
could definitely see

00:26:50.750 --> 00:26:55.550
that she had a huge box of
antidiarrheal medication,

00:26:55.550 --> 00:26:59.183
just out there, in front of everybody.

00:27:00.698 --> 00:27:01.890
And Christy's putting it away,

00:27:01.890 --> 00:27:03.830
after, at the end of our whole meal,

00:27:03.830 --> 00:27:05.780
after being there for like two hours.

00:27:05.780 --> 00:27:07.350
And we're talking to the guy about it,

00:27:07.350 --> 00:27:08.705
and he's like,

00:27:08.705 --> 00:27:11.440
"Yeah, I saw that, but I
didn't want to say anything."

00:27:11.440 --> 00:27:14.135
So it's, even though I don't know,

00:27:14.135 --> 00:27:14.968
it just wouldn't leave us.

00:27:14.968 --> 00:27:15.801
Like it was just,

00:27:15.801 --> 00:27:17.200
the diarrhea was a specter.

00:27:17.200 --> 00:27:18.530
Well, yeah, you need to be ready.

00:27:18.530 --> 00:27:21.300
There were, we ate at that, we had a,

00:27:21.300 --> 00:27:23.850
just a coffee at that place.

00:27:23.850 --> 00:27:25.836
It's a cool spot, man.

00:27:25.836 --> 00:27:28.560
And it's a very wild bird,

00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:31.490
that was very aggressively
eating people's food-

00:27:31.490 --> 00:27:32.323
Oh, there wasn't one of those.

00:27:32.323 --> 00:27:33.810
Off of their table.

00:27:33.810 --> 00:27:36.190
They must have shot him.
Must have killed him.

00:27:36.190 --> 00:27:37.560
I might have been eating him.

00:27:37.560 --> 00:27:40.050
I ate a chicken sandwich.
Yeah.

00:27:40.050 --> 00:27:41.290
Next day,

00:27:41.290 --> 00:27:44.360
we got up and there was
no rain in the forecast,

00:27:44.360 --> 00:27:45.193
for that day.

00:27:45.193 --> 00:27:46.026
So I'm like, all right,

00:27:46.026 --> 00:27:48.530
today's the day that we're
going to go down by the river.

00:27:48.530 --> 00:27:50.460
And again, no hiking.

00:27:50.460 --> 00:27:55.010
We're going to go in full
meditative retreat mode.

00:27:55.010 --> 00:27:58.560
They take these Adirondack
chairs, are you familiar?

00:27:58.560 --> 00:27:59.780
Yeah, I believe so.

00:27:59.780 --> 00:28:00.730
Well, describe it.

00:28:00.730 --> 00:28:04.171
Adirondack chair, to me, is one of those,

00:28:04.171 --> 00:28:05.660
it's high backed, made out of wood.

00:28:05.660 --> 00:28:06.753
Yeah.

00:28:06.753 --> 00:28:07.930
You just kind of leans back a little bit.

00:28:07.930 --> 00:28:09.389
Yeah.

00:28:09.389 --> 00:28:10.222
And you're kind of low to the ground.

00:28:10.222 --> 00:28:11.196
Uh-huh.

00:28:11.196 --> 00:28:13.194
They had taken pairs of those,

00:28:13.194 --> 00:28:15.113
and put them in the Big Sur river,

00:28:16.120 --> 00:28:19.000
because the river is basically
just a really wide stream.

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:19.833
And there's lots of places

00:28:19.833 --> 00:28:21.690
where you can just sit on the rocks.

00:28:21.690 --> 00:28:24.570
So we just went down
there and sat for a while,

00:28:24.570 --> 00:28:27.133
and did nothing.
Feet in the water?

00:28:28.120 --> 00:28:29.550
Too cold for that.

00:28:29.550 --> 00:28:31.220
I was like, I'm going to
get totally ready for this.

00:28:31.220 --> 00:28:33.480
I'm gonna put on my new sweatshirt.

00:28:33.480 --> 00:28:34.950
I don't know if you noticed

00:28:34.950 --> 00:28:36.330
This, this, this is the moment.

00:28:36.330 --> 00:28:38.100
This is the moment where
you explain your sweatshirt.

00:28:38.100 --> 00:28:41.510
I ordered this thing off an Instagram ad,

00:28:41.510 --> 00:28:43.940
shout out to my friend, Todd Snyder,

00:28:43.940 --> 00:28:46.289
teaming up with LLB.

00:28:46.289 --> 00:28:47.720
It makes quite a statement.

00:28:47.720 --> 00:28:52.720
I'm like, I think this is,
how do you say, ironic?

00:28:53.260 --> 00:28:55.250
But not really.

00:28:55.250 --> 00:28:59.530
It kind of says, I
don't really go camping,

00:28:59.530 --> 00:29:00.880
but I like the idea of camping.

00:29:00.880 --> 00:29:01.713
Yes.

00:29:04.443 --> 00:29:08.040
And this isn't, I think this is Maine.

00:29:08.040 --> 00:29:09.840
You know, you got some ducks flying.

00:29:10.800 --> 00:29:12.540
You got some fall foliage,

00:29:12.540 --> 00:29:15.000
going all the way down
the sleeves on this thing.

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:16.440
Yeah. It's quite a print.

00:29:16.440 --> 00:29:17.280
That's not easy to do.

00:29:17.280 --> 00:29:20.430
I did get a compliment or two for it.

00:29:20.430 --> 00:29:21.960
Hmm.

00:29:21.960 --> 00:29:23.660
What were the, what did they say?

00:29:23.660 --> 00:29:24.493
Nice sweatshirt?

00:29:24.493 --> 00:29:25.326
I think it was something like,

00:29:25.326 --> 00:29:26.159
what did he say?

00:29:26.159 --> 00:29:27.200
We were in one of these like little,

00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:29.050
you'll find a little bookstore,

00:29:29.050 --> 00:29:30.630
They got a lot of little-
on the edge of the...

00:29:30.630 --> 00:29:33.810
With some like philosophical stuff.

00:29:33.810 --> 00:29:36.217
People doing a lot of
introspection up in that place.

00:29:36.217 --> 00:29:37.050
Yeah.

00:29:37.050 --> 00:29:41.610
I think he said something
like, "That Sweatshirt is hot",

00:29:41.610 --> 00:29:42.940
not hot, maybe he was like-

00:29:42.940 --> 00:29:44.473
Mm. Fire.

00:29:44.473 --> 00:29:45.430
I don't think he said, no cap.

00:29:45.430 --> 00:29:46.290
I can't remember.

00:29:46.290 --> 00:29:47.914
Who was this guy?

00:29:47.914 --> 00:29:49.050
He was just a dude who seemed cool.

00:29:49.050 --> 00:29:49.883
How old?

00:29:49.883 --> 00:29:51.150
He was a little younger than me.

00:29:51.150 --> 00:29:52.438
Huh.

00:29:52.438 --> 00:29:53.271
So?
Okay.

00:29:53.271 --> 00:29:54.390
I think it, it worked for him.

00:29:54.390 --> 00:29:56.340
It definitely worked for me,

00:29:56.340 --> 00:29:58.530
and I got the photos to prove it.

00:29:58.530 --> 00:30:00.770
So here I am sitting in the Big Sur river,

00:30:00.770 --> 00:30:01.870
in an Adirondack chair,

00:30:01.870 --> 00:30:04.190
wearing my turtle neck sweatshirt.

00:30:04.190 --> 00:30:05.898
Where were the feet?

00:30:05.898 --> 00:30:06.940
The main scene.

00:30:06.940 --> 00:30:08.180
They were on the rocks.

00:30:08.180 --> 00:30:09.013
It was just too,

00:30:09.013 --> 00:30:10.200
it was a little too cold.

00:30:10.200 --> 00:30:11.162
But okay.

00:30:11.162 --> 00:30:12.960
Put your feet in the water.
It's not in the water,

00:30:12.960 --> 00:30:14.911
